Worksheet (r04.html)

F1: Game class holds all state; SeededRandom (mulberry32-style) used everywhere (genMap, genPeople, fireEvent, spawnCaravan) with no Math.random found; endTurn() runs 9 numbered fixed-order steps. All parts present. Score 2.

F2: genMap() builds 8x8 (map.length 64) from this.rng; canBuild() checks tile.terrain === building.terrain. getAdjacent()/adjacency bonus text only appears in showTileTooltip() (cosmetic) - never read in the endTurn production loop, so it never changes production numbers. Missing required part. Score 1.

F3: GREENHOUSE requires water:1 (consumed) to produce food:3, water supplied by CONDENSER - real input->output chain; storage_caps enforced with explicit overflow log+clamp in endTurn production loop. FORGE (ore+power in, production:[]) is a dead-end but the water->food chain and cap/overflow handling are real. Score 2.

F4: people[] records carry skill/fatigue/morale/experience; assignWorker() sets this.assigned + building.assigned_worker, read in endTurn as worker.skill/worker.fatigue/worker.morale to compute output_mult. All parts present. Score 2.

F5: food_need/water_need computed per turn in endTurn(); shortage reduces p.morale for all colonists; worker.morale<50 multiplies output_mult by 0.7 in production loop; morale is not an instant kill (partial penalty) and can recover via events/morale-focus research. Score 2.

F6: RESEARCH_TREE has 8 nodes; queueResearch() enforces config.prereqs and deducts cost. 6/8 nodes have a real applied effect (research_done['better-farming']/'advanced-parts'/'research-lab' checked directly in production loop; storm-shelter cuts storm_dmg; morale-focus adds morale regen; power-gen/research-lab unlock buildings via BUILDINGS[x].research=null). water-retention (water_cap_mult) and ore-refining (ore_to_metal_mult) effect functions are defined but never called or read anywhere - dead code, no gameplay effect. Score 1.

F7: event_list has 10 entries, each with 2 choices with differing state effects (>=4 qualify, e.g. Treasure Cache, Settler Arrival, Water Contamination, Ore Deposit). Selection is `available[Math.floor(rng.next()*available.length)]` - uniform, no per-event weight field exists, so "weighted random selection" is absent. events_cooldown[name]=turn+10 is set but never compared against turn anywhere (no `turn >= cooldown` check) - it only acts as a fired/not-fired flag cleared in bulk when all events are exhausted, not a real per-turn cooldown. Two required parts missing. Score 1.

F8: spawnCaravan() prices read `this.resources[item]/this.storage_caps[item]` (player stockpile) into supply_mod; caravan_inventory[item] is finite and decremented on buy (qty capped by stock); tradeWith() implements both buy and sell branches, both mutate resources/scrip. All parts present. Score 2.

F9: turn%8===0 fires storms; storm_severity += 0.5/turn and feeds storm_dmg_base; storm-shelter research cuts storm_dmg *0.6; repair step spends 5 parts/building and restores health. But building.health is never read in the production loop (endTurn step 2) - damaged buildings produce at full rate, only tile opacity changes in updateUI(). Explicitly the "at most 1" case per the rubric note. Score 1.

F10: No save/export function, no textarea/copy UI, no import/parse function anywhere in the file. serializeState()/hashState() exist only for devRunTests/devBenchmark, never exposed to the player. Absent. Score 0.

F11: endTurn() step 9 checks `people.length===0` (lose, reachable via morale decay) and `turn>=60 && people.length>=12` (win, reachable via Settler Arrival growing pop from starting 8); endGame() computes score from people.length, research_done count, food+water+parts, turn; renders #endGameModal with title/text. All parts present. Score 2.

F12: switchTab() toggles .tab/.panel active classes, wired to 6 generated tab buttons; log entries render `T${entry.turn}:` prefix; showTileTooltip() explains terrain/health/buildable options (though its adjacency-bonus line reflects a value never applied to production, see F2); keydown handler binds Space and Digit1-5 (Dev tab has no shortcut); @media(max-width:600px) reflows .content/.map-grid/.tabs. Score 2.

F13: devRunTests() has 15 assertions, most real invariants (resource>=0, resource<=cap, health 0-100, skill 1-5, fatigue 0-100, serialize/hash roundtrip); a couple are tautological (people.length>=0, turn>=0, always true in JS). devBenchmark() builds `new Game()` and loops sim.endTurn() 200 times and prints hashState() output, but Game's constructor/newGame/endTurn all call updateUI(), which touches the live DOM (#stats, #turn, #mapGrid, same ids as the visible game) every simulated turn - not actually headless. Required part missing. Score 1.

G1: research_done['better-farming']/'advanced-parts'/'research-lab' are read directly inside the per-building production loop in endTurn() and multiply `amount` before it's added to state.resources, every turn a matching building exists and produces. Visible immediately in the stats panel. Score 4.

G2: food_need/water_need shortfall in endTurn() step 1 subtracts from all p.morale; production loop step 2 reads worker.morale (<50 -> output_mult*=0.7). Full pipeline wired every turn, but the effect is a binary threshold at 50 rather than continuous scaling. Score 3.

G3: endTurn() step 4 (turn%8===0) sets this.buildings[idx].health -= storm_dmg; step 5 repairs health by spending parts. But building.health is never read anywhere in the production loop (step 2) - damaged buildings produce at full rate. Per the rubric's explicit "storms damage buildings but damaged buildings produce at full rate -> at most 1" case. Score 1.

G4: spawnCaravan() computes caravan_prices[item] from `1 + (this.resources[item]/this.storage_caps[item])*0.5`, i.e. reads live player stockpile, recomputed each time a caravan spawns (every 15 turns) and displayed/used in tradeWith(). Real formula reading state, but only refreshed at spawn rather than continuously drifting. Score 3.

G5: fireEvent() choice actions durably mutate state, not just log: Treasure Cache adds resources.scrip/parts; Settler Arrival pushes a new person into this.people (population growth) conditioned on food cost; Water Contamination/Ore Deposit/Illness/Skill Growth similarly write resources, people[].morale, or people[].skill directly. Score 4.

